; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6540  
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6541  \ID                SBSW_COMM_CHANNEL_CSL02
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6542  \DESCRIPTION       Access to an array that has a size relation to ComM_Channel.
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6543  \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL02 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6544  
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6545  \ID                SBSW_COMM_ARRAY_CHANNEL_WRITE
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6546  \DESCRIPTION       Write access to an array of size COMM_ACTIVE_CHANNEL.
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6547  \COUNTERMEASURE \N A preprocessor check ensures that COMM_ACTIVE_CHANNEL == ComM_GetSizeOfChannel(). The reason is that some channel-based arrays are
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6548                     defined locally in this file and some are defined using the ComStackLib. The check is needed to ensure that arrays have the same size.
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6549                     For all implementation variant ComM_GetSizeOfChannel() is always defined to a constant number.
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6550                     If used in a for loop, the array index is always smaller than ComM_GetSizeOfChannel(). If a function parameter
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6551                     is used as array index, the validity is ensured by a DET check.
; ..\BSW\ComM\ComM.c	  6552  
